cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If Scan2CAD contributes to your work, a software citation is appreciated. Citation is optional."
type: software
title: "Scan2CAD: Guided Reverse Engineering of 3D Scans to STEP"
authors:
  - family-names: "Lanz"
    given-names: "Amon P."
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AmLanz/Scan2CAD"
url: "https://github.com/AmLanz/Scan2CAD"
abstract: "Python desktop tool that turns 3D scans (STL/OBJ/PLY) into closed STEP solids through guided reverse engineering: feature fitting, holes and turned profiles, symmetries and constraints, and an exact scan-topology B-rep with a feature-to-STEP check. Developed with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)."
keywords:
  - reverse engineering
  - 3D scanning
  - STEP
  - CAD
  - OpenCASCADE
  - Python
